*Blocker:* a path beyond the two; a product byte; the counts blob changed or the verify pair not 5102/306 (either direction); a stand-in that answers any URL other than the exact one, or answers after `goto`; the guard PASSING a genuinely banner-less/invisible setup or status page with the stand-in on (Check 2d); `waitUntil` or a timeout changed; a NEW CodeQL alert with security severity high+ or rule severity `error`, or a `CodeQL` check-run concluded failure; a merge-result tree other than main plus the two files; a gitleaks finding; a person name, decision-card id or secret in the message/title/body; the head moved. *Major (class named on the line, "NO GO 1 of 2"):* a surviving mutant M1-M5 or M7 (the cell does not pin the URL, the count or the placement); a stand-in whose count is not asserted per page; a with-versus-without difference in banner box, contrast or ink; a builder claim contradicted by your measurement that changes the basis (a blob, the 66 titles, the census 1/1/ten 0, the red/green harness rows); `Build` red at the head for a reason not shown to be a base fact. *Minor/Note:* M8, M9 (the response shape unpinned); M6; the PR body's Opus trailer; a ticket key in a message; node version differing from CI; the `mergeable_state` text; `cdn.jsdelivr.net` still a third-party dependency of eleven pages (RD-721; not in the ruling); the cell's `r.m.standIn` read when a measurement threw (read the job's error path and say what the cell then prints; Note unless it hides the cause).
